From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:22:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delegate): a subagent's question outlives its chat's
 memory; a child's error names its exception

A background subagent ended with status=error and the parent's session id
as its whole error. A subagent keeps running after its parent chat left the
gateway's memory (an idle conversation retires, a restarted gateway starts
without it) and asks a question or an approval later. Registering that
prompt with the viewers read `authority.sessions[<parent session id>]` and
raised KeyError inside the child's tool call; str(KeyError(id)) is only the
id, so the parent read it as the error. Same lookup in the clarify path
after the answer.

Registering a subagent's prompt now restores a retired conversation, and
when it cannot be restored (a restart of a local conversation, a deleted
one) logs a warning and leaves only the viewers' copy unregistered: the
chat adapter already shows the card and takes the answer.

A child that raises now reports `Type: message (at file:line in function)`;
a KeyError says `KeyError: missing key '<key>'`, never the bare key.
